<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Obock</h1><p class="st-meta">1862 CE – 1896 CE · capital Obock</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">France's first foothold on the Gulf of Aden, a small coaling station that grew into the colony of French Somaliland and modern Djibouti.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1862 French agents bought the anchorage of Obock on the northern shore of the Gulf of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-tadjoura">Tadjoura</a> from local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afar">Afar</a> rulers for 10,000 thalers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> had little use for it until the 1880s, when the opening of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain's</a> refusal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> French ships at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> made a French base necessary.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 1884 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonce-lagarde">Leonce Lagarde</a> became commandant and expanded French influence by treaties with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-tadjoura">Sultanate of Tadjoura</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/issa-clan">Issa Somali</a> clans. Obock served as a coaling and supply station for French ships bound for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">Indochina</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. Its harbour was poor, and its trade was small.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonce-lagarde">Lagarde</a> founded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/djibouti">Djibouti</a> across the gulf in 1888, which offered a better port and access to the Ethiopian trade. In 1896 the capital moved there and Obock became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-somaliland">French Somaliland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/obock.jpg" alt="Obock" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Luc Michel · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Obock,_Djibouti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1862 CE – 1896 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Obock</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Leonce Lagarde</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Afar, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/djibouti">Djibouti</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Obock Territory, Territoire d'Obock</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1879&amp;focus=obock" aria-label="Obock on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5870 1731 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Obock lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6190 1987L5054 728M6190 1987L6187 2001"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M6187 2001h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6190 1987h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6190 1987h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1879&amp;focus=obock">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
